      "source": "SAC Route Portal",
      "notes_html": "<p>On the ascent to Oberbauenstock there is a steep schrofen and rock face with scrambling passages (T4+, fixed ropes), followed by a sometimes precipitous grass and schrofen ridge (T4). The ascent to Niderbauen Chulm is easier: T3+ with a few protected passages, a ladder and a very steep grassy slope. The orientation is unproblematic, but the tour is not for wet days.</p>"
